WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.688
Day two is run by the people who touch
the estate most and decide the least.

2
00:00:04.688 --> 00:00:08.413
So every decision has to sit with
someone who isn't at the keyboard.

3
00:00:08.413 --> 00:00:13.149
A desk that approves its own resets
has rebuilt the standing administrator.

4
00:00:13.149 --> 00:00:16.338
The book separates
deciding, doing and owning.

5
00:00:16.338 --> 00:00:17.812
The desk executes.

6
00:00:17.812 --> 00:00:22.687
Its supervisor approves only routine
credential work for ordinary users.

7
00:00:22.687 --> 00:00:27.394
Platform owners own the runbooks;
control owners own the approval gates;

8
00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:30.688
the platform team builds
both and decides neither.

9
00:00:30.688 --> 00:00:36.341
And because runbooks decay, the decision
for the CIO is to give every catalog item,

10
00:00:36.341 --> 00:00:40.138
runbook and workflow one
named owner and a review date.

11
00:00:40.138 --> 00:00:41.710
Next, measuring it.
